   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT in relation to permitting the Unitarian Universalist Congregation of\nthe Great South Bay Sayville to file an application for a real property tax\nexemption",
    "basePrintNo": "S6460",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6460-2019",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Real Property Taxation",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S6460\n\nSPONSOR: MARTINEZ\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act in relation to permitting the Unitarian Univer-\nsalist Congregation of the Great South Bay Sayville to file an applica-\ntion for a real property tax exemption\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA:\n\nTo authorize the assessor of the Town of Islip to accept from the Unita-\nrian Universalist Congregation of the Great South Bay Sayville, an\napplication for exemption from real property taxes from the 2016-2017,\nand 2017-2018 assessment roles.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection One of the bill authorizes the Town of Islip, county of Suffolk,\nto accept from the Unitarian Universalist Congregation of the Great\nSouth Bay Sayville, a not-for-profit organization, an application for an\nexemption of real property taxes for the parcel located at 11 Collins\nAvenue in Sayville, New York, otherwise known as district 0500, section\n383.00, block 02.00, lot 001.000 in the Town of Islip, county of Suffolk\nfor the 2016-2017, 2017-2018 tax rolls.  Upon satisfaction that the\nchurch would have otherwise been entitled to said exemption, the asses-\nsor may grant this exemption upon approval of the town board. Further,\nthe board, in its sole discretion, may provide for the refund of taxes\npaid and cancel taxes, fines, penalties, liens, or interest remaining\nunpaid.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nExisting law authorizes tax exemptions to be granted after the taxable\nstatus date as passed if a bill is chaptered authorizing an assessor to\naccept a late application.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nA10144 of 2017/2018: Referred to Rules\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS\n\nNone to the State.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis bill shall take effect immediately.\n",
